    {
      "CVE": "CVE-2026-75818",
      "Description": "GNU Aspell prezip-bin contains a heap-based buffer overflow vulnerability in the decompressor in prog/prezip.c. The decompressor does not properly check buffer space, so a crafted compressed file can cause out-of-bounds read and write operations on the heap. An attacker who convinces a user to process a malicious compressed file with prezip-bin can trigger memory corruption, leading to a processs crash.\n\n\n\nThis issue was fixed in commit  15b188437f9e0192d4ac4472ad66a4e2f62a782f which will be  released in version  0.60.8.3.",
      "Threats": [
        {
          "Type": "Impact",
          "Severity": "moderate"
        }
      ],
      "References": [
